<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Westpac plans 85 mln share buyback.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Westpac plans 85 mln share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westpac Banking Corp said on Monday it planned the on-market buyback of up to five percent of its ordinary shares, or about 85 million shares, through to May next year.  </p>
<p>Westpac said the buyback scheme to be conducted by brokerage firm Ord Minnett would begin on November 18 this year and end on May 17 next year.</p>
<p>It said the scheme was designed to optimise the major bank's capital efficiency.</p>
<p>Westpac shares were 11 cents higher at a year's high of A$7.29 at 1.40 p.m. (0240 GMT).</p>
<p>The bank's shares have a year's low of A$5.20.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
